{"version":"2.1.0","runs":[{"invocations":[{"executionSuccessful":true,"toolExecutionNotifications":[]}],"results":[{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"b1959de777033a446c9922f2600ab35d530672c345da24d9bf0475b3a47ad84576b4d2a02fdecbd217785ddc771e2c330b0d697884d67d0e5c8007f368fd84e5_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":49,"endLine":53,"snippet":{"text":"    size_t bytes = (size_t) Long_val(vwords) * 8;"},"startColumn":20,"startLine":53}}}],"message":{"text":"Mapping byte length is computed as (size_t)Long_val(words) * 8 without an overflow check. A large words count wraps size_t, under-allocates the mmap, and later region stores walk off the mapping (SIGBUS / corruption). Reject words that would overflow or use a checked multiply before mmap/ftruncate.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-map-size-overflow"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"1a885f3c8c18bf69aa13759e43b6e7436c2ecd7a1ba3255e378fe3a708148e3230c1131ed9a8dae85d9bde4bea187597bd29b24eefff126cb1e8964752b92c2c_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":62,"endLine":62,"snippet":{"text":"        int oflag = O_RDWR | (Bool_val(vcreate) ? O_CREAT : 0);"},"startColumn":21,"startLine":62}}}],"message":{"text":"shm_open create path uses O_CREAT without O_EXCL. A second creator (or a retry after a crash) opens the existing object and may ftruncate it under live peers — two logical sessions share one name. Require O_CREAT|O_EXCL for exclusive create, or open existing read-only and validate generation/size before joining.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-shm-create-without-excl"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"7663f989761de78269d8eaa78a75caa1764eb074f0a1f17351fd81b81fe6abe8e6d1d3a8263648f940f353a417818ad5873fc936b994289310a5de60a5a88c40_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":55,"endLine":64,"snippet":{"text":"        if (fd < 0) caml_failwith(\"qr_map: shm_open\");"},"startColumn":9,"startLine":64}}}],"message":{"text":"caml_failwith with a fixed string discards errno (and QNX's error detail). Callers see \"MsgSendv\" / \"shm_open\" with no strerror, which makes EAGAIN vs EINTR vs EBADF indistinguishable — the pulse EAGAIN crash is the sharp edge of this pattern. Prefer caml_uerror / caml_unix_error, or include strerror(errno) in the message.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-failwith-discards-errno"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"b5693c5b54a9084af38bc010c6011078097d866a7f948b42b8817324f5fab0b92ca94ecbe7f1327828153f41ad5fc9846fb61625db98d8d263bef79871d154c7_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":62,"endLine":65,"snippet":{"text":"        if (Bool_val(vcreate) && ftruncate(fd, (off_t) bytes) != 0) {"},"startColumn":34,"startLine":65}}}],"message":{"text":"ftruncate on a shm_open fd with O_CREAT but without O_EXCL: if the shared object already exists (e.g. a previous run or another participant sized it differently), this silently resizes shared state other processes may be using — stale/partial mappings, SIGBUS, or silent data loss. Use O_EXCL for create, or fstat and verify the existing size before truncating.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-ftruncate-resizes-shared-object"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"f8f020d5d5ea58e329bc2a3bd568da0dcc7996e88d82db5db2f7b0020c5bc369a8a8ebfbfb61941280f3e6210243a4c53ed414a77dab4725c4cabfab985aba38_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":41,"endLine":70,"snippet":{"text":"    if (hint != NULL) flags |= MAP_FIXED;"},"startColumn":23,"startLine":70}}}],"message":{"text":"MAP_FIXED silently replaces any existing mapping overlapping the requested range — a wrong hint address can destroy the process's own address space with no error. Prefer MAP_FIXED_NOREPLACE (check EEXIST) or verify the range is free before mapping.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-map-fixed-silent-overwrite"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"8976c621ad185e45f3af95df00018323c2fdab69f1ef99521fc5d4d6e140c7333e6ae4c2f4563ceaeacdd6fd747a62834bba147fe80db08469277998ee69cda2_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":65,"endLine":72,"snippet":{"text":"    p = mmap(hint, bytes, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE, flags, fd, 0);"},"startColumn":5,"startLine":72}}}],"message":{"text":"mmap without a matching munmap in the same function. On the success path the Bigarray may own the mapping for the process lifetime, but any failure after a successful mmap (or a missing custom finalizer) leaks the virtual mapping. Pair error paths with munmap, and ensure GC finalization calls munmap when the region is released.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-mmap-without-munmap"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"ef7b3670a9763c5ce6debdfbd86c5f9f80012723a42f08cd45ec670b825587713cb9a4dd095cfa7d813d0f7a4e6f5cfb324b58c3288c984d56907d9b1b0a7331_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":64,"endLine":72,"snippet":{"text":"    p = mmap(hint, bytes, PROT_READ | PROT_WRITE, flags, fd, 0);"},"startColumn":9,"startLine":72}}}],"message":{"text":"shm_open → mmap without an fstat size check between them. If the creator sized the object differently (code skew, partial create, or a new generation under the same name), mmap succeeds and the first touch past st_size delivers SIGBUS. fstat and require st_size >= expected bytes before mapping; on mismatch unmap/retry or fail cleanly.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-attach-without-fstat-size"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"6017e101fef213ea647899438567e0a009ea78e2c3d5e67154390b58b31ce54434071e93f4d73e8c72c3a54be0500ca6e4a72bf84d296d2e601f7f165b2f8df2_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":56,"endLine":74,"snippet":{"text":"    if (p == MAP_FAILED) caml_failwith(\"qr_map: mmap\");"},"startColumn":5,"startLine":74}}}],"message":{"text":"caml_failwith with a fixed string discards errno (and QNX's error detail). Callers see \"MsgSendv\" / \"shm_open\" with no strerror, which makes EAGAIN vs EINTR vs EBADF indistinguishable — the pulse EAGAIN crash is the sharp edge of this pattern. Prefer caml_uerror / caml_unix_error, or include strerror(errno) in the message.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-failwith-discards-errno"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"15ebd00b8e4c4c21992163b01e0581ed681a47490c5df61ccc3b5bd43228fe2572152b897aeb245a0e42e34be37d5ac7eb239876c2cc271e5fd3f5c608028b7b_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":30,"endLine":120,"snippet":{"text":"    return caml_copy_int64(x);"},"startColumn":12,"startLine":120}}}],"message":{"text":"caml_copy_int64 boxes an int64 on the OCaml heap. In load_acq / fetch_add this fires on every ring push/pop and vclock tick — the C side of the \"zero OCaml heap allocation in steady state\" hole. Expose [@@unboxed] externals (int64_t in/out) so the stub returns a raw integer without allocating.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-caml-copy-int64-hot-path"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"15ebd00b8e4c4c21992163b01e0581ed681a47490c5df61ccc3b5bd43228fe2572152b897aeb245a0e42e34be37d5ac7eb239876c2cc271e5fd3f5c608028b7b_1"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":30,"endLine":135,"snippet":{"text":"    return caml_copy_int64(x);"},"startColumn":12,"startLine":135}}}],"message":{"text":"caml_copy_int64 boxes an int64 on the OCaml heap. In load_acq / fetch_add this fires on every ring push/pop and vclock tick — the C side of the \"zero OCaml heap allocation in steady state\" hole. Expose [@@unboxed] externals (int64_t in/out) so the stub returns a raw integer without allocating.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-caml-copy-int64-hot-path"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"3afa6a700af92b5577c6fcc66abd5ec603d3a2712ca08c8f4edf55f6189ee153381554d031380b0afd9bc8d40a13cd1327d7fa2ed7963730f765200187df3f5e_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":57,"endLine":152,"snippet":{"text":"    if (clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &ts) != 0)\n        caml_failwith(\"clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC)\");"},"startColumn":5,"startLine":151}}}],"message":{"text":"caml_failwith with a fixed string discards errno (and QNX's error detail). Callers see \"MsgSendv\" / \"shm_open\" with no strerror, which makes EAGAIN vs EINTR vs EBADF indistinguishable — the pulse EAGAIN crash is the sharp edge of this pattern. Prefer caml_uerror / caml_unix_error, or include strerror(errno) in the message.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-failwith-discards-errno"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"b30a554e7e9d363159b696431acd073cf28d8afd61a8aca906c5f4fecbef740c3f214ce6f9275545eaadf1c379fef8537bcf327f73b8f81e9f7304d1750375c0_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":50,"endLine":177,"snippet":{"text":"    if (chid < 0) caml_failwith(\"ChannelCreate\");"},"startColumn":5,"startLine":177}}}],"message":{"text":"caml_failwith with a fixed string discards errno (and QNX's error detail). Callers see \"MsgSendv\" / \"shm_open\" with no strerror, which makes EAGAIN vs EINTR vs EBADF indistinguishable — the pulse EAGAIN crash is the sharp edge of this pattern. Prefer caml_uerror / caml_unix_error, or include strerror(errno) in the message.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-failwith-discards-errno"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"d2412c5127b3f13f6da9d2f4c43935b8e9d71068b171ad18757e532549221ac7872617c12f8e7669f05dc2bb65dec6c305effc319dc5797b7a4dfc0709c08380_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":50,"endLine":185,"snippet":{"text":"    if (coid < 0) caml_failwith(\"ConnectAttach\");"},"startColumn":5,"startLine":185}}}],"message":{"text":"ConnectAttach failure is reported only as caml_failwith(\"ConnectAttach\"), discarding errno. ESRCH/EINVAL here is the stale-session signal (dead producer pid/chid published in a previous generation). Return the error to OCaml so the caller can drop the mapping, munmap, and retry/remap against a fresh READY publication instead of crashing the joiner.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-connect-attach-discards-errno"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"9cd4e03c3355341da616189b221d71e082a0c11832240b84492b8d55dc93f519bde59756be1ae1d5a00deb08142c961eaa1a39053e04d70afe2501b8f0179068_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":55,"endLine":206,"snippet":{"text":"    rc = MsgSendv(Long_val(vcoid), &siov, 1, &riov, 1);"},"startColumn":10,"startLine":206}}}],"message":{"text":"MsgSendv collects the reply into a stack-local buffer that is never read — the reply payload is silently discarded (the comment suggests a caller buffer). Either return the reply words to OCaml or shrink the reply iov to zero and document that sends are ack-only.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-msgsendv-reply-discarded"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"409f05f01f2462729d080cb7fe8b6c857f5ab0fc0be8b8150a5cc6b9e1bd141abf07098c276fcbdf2f57c4424b2b95f5306187cbd640757c089081a291a479f6_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":43,"endLine":208,"snippet":{"text":"    if (rc < 0) caml_failwith(\"MsgSendv\");"},"startColumn":5,"startLine":208}}}],"message":{"text":"caml_failwith with a fixed string discards errno (and QNX's error detail). Callers see \"MsgSendv\" / \"shm_open\" with no strerror, which makes EAGAIN vs EINTR vs EBADF indistinguishable — the pulse EAGAIN crash is the sharp edge of this pattern. Prefer caml_uerror / caml_unix_error, or include strerror(errno) in the message.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-failwith-discards-errno"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"1ed529342901774ccbb14baba15e1a3c48bfb3c1f813ffac2653927ac8db586529c8ead02227fdf63365d1f52ddfc47284ca6d355e5acf42a79184c52112c2c4_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":35,"endLine":241,"snippet":{"text":"    if (MsgReply(Long_val(vrcvid), Long_val(vstatus), NULL, 0) < 0)\n        caml_failwith(\"MsgReply\");"},"startColumn":5,"startLine":240}}}],"message":{"text":"caml_failwith with a fixed string discards errno (and QNX's error detail). Callers see \"MsgSendv\" / \"shm_open\" with no strerror, which makes EAGAIN vs EINTR vs EBADF indistinguishable — the pulse EAGAIN crash is the sharp edge of this pattern. Prefer caml_uerror / caml_unix_error, or include strerror(errno) in the message.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-failwith-discards-errno"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"d21f22a50cbd90739a27c8c78cd888ad68d078ca3e1c70bbd693d6ff4fe5d827feb6fb5830ee3c8bc73f89570914ab22a618dee8142c3cce39592c9a85c91095_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":44,"endLine":263,"snippet":{"text":"    if (rc < 0) caml_failwith(\"MsgReplyv\");"},"startColumn":5,"startLine":263}}}],"message":{"text":"caml_failwith with a fixed string discards errno (and QNX's error detail). Callers see \"MsgSendv\" / \"shm_open\" with no strerror, which makes EAGAIN vs EINTR vs EBADF indistinguishable — the pulse EAGAIN crash is the sharp edge of this pattern. Prefer caml_uerror / caml_unix_error, or include strerror(errno) in the message.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-failwith-discards-errno"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"ec2d00373fb156e1884b7aca1a90a2916d5ed46bc4c805695b4829543af4cf3511d17b26cb869a45754c299356bdd3df3429419db9b3c4c68cb07676d0ea585d_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":46,"endLine":279,"snippet":{"text":"    if (rc < 0) caml_failwith(\"MsgSendPulse\");"},"startColumn":17,"startLine":279}}}],"message":{"text":"MsgSendPulse fails with EAGAIN when the receiver's pulse pool is exhausted; failing hard turns backpressure (producer spin-waiting on a full ring, pulsing every retry) into a producer crash. Return the error to OCaml and let the caller rate-limit or coalesce wakeups.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-pulse-eagain-crashes-producer"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"78571a04806c449ce4ec74eae810d6122508a38b9f39b7ecf6893abe4d8906ef79390f28aa6807e50effe0ab20f5f532e3719a5c3483a923dcf85f2a3b3d57da_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":60,"endLine":295,"snippet":{"text":"    if (pthread_setschedparam(pthread_self(), SCHED_FIFO, &p) != 0)\n        caml_failwith(\"pthread_setschedparam(SCHED_FIFO)\");"},"startColumn":5,"startLine":294}}}],"message":{"text":"caml_failwith with a fixed string discards errno (and QNX's error detail). Callers see \"MsgSendv\" / \"shm_open\" with no strerror, which makes EAGAIN vs EINTR vs EBADF indistinguishable — the pulse EAGAIN crash is the sharp edge of this pattern. Prefer caml_uerror / caml_unix_error, or include strerror(errno) in the message.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-failwith-discards-errno"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"43d9499ed40dc81d7ea971325a9a068c20ffc19bc79649e2a076a0c578105677cec57cbb9fd36d82ebff9ad6e2a9731c1b66f5e6e092ccfeb009ec0e6206a99d_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":53,"endLine":302,"snippet":{"text":"    uintptr_t mask = (uintptr_t) 1 << Long_val(vcpu);"},"startColumn":22,"startLine":302}}}],"message":{"text":"Shift amount comes straight from an OCaml value with no range check; cpu >= 64 is undefined behavior. Clamp or validate before shifting.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-unchecked-shift-amount"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"dbc288b662ea8d9cc421c0e5d51e046d9749bca3c86d104c17815d765541c2867aecbe934be2600b6c182e72d38966265da46f71cceee1121ec97fce5e6eb99f_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"/tmp/qnxml_stubs_scan.c","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":55,"endLine":304,"snippet":{"text":"    if (ThreadCtl(_NTO_TCTL_RUNMASK, (void *) mask) != 0)\n        caml_failwith(\"ThreadCtl(_NTO_TCTL_RUNMASK)\");"},"startColumn":5,"startLine":303}}}],"message":{"text":"caml_failwith with a fixed string discards errno (and QNX's error detail). Callers see \"MsgSendv\" / \"shm_open\" with no strerror, which makes EAGAIN vs EINTR vs EBADF indistinguishable — the pulse EAGAIN crash is the sharp edge of this pattern. Prefer caml_uerror / caml_unix_error, or include strerror(errno) in the message.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-failwith-discards-errno"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"ddd86278274878894d0e4433d7aac1270309ae1abdaf924eedfefa0f576ecea00e50a47e9b1cdb90b0b1ba74ea844318827b29e18687ad1782bfa74b25eee78c_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"demo/consumer.ml","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":45,"endLine":52,"snippet":{"text":"      checksum := Int64.add !checksum out.{1};"},"startColumn":19,"startLine":52}}}],"message":{"text":"Int64 arithmetic returns a freshly boxed int64. On hot paths (ring push/pop staging, merkle mix/update, demo tight loops) each add/mul/ sub/logxor is a minor allocation on top of any of_int boxing. Prefer unboxed int64 externals or keep heavy mixers off the steady-state path if the zero-allocation claim must hold strictly.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-int64-arith-hot-path"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"46ba230ed670c3dee25a87d5f650b9df093f166f1fd39f74149dbda656346076b0582177b941d2a68e198333a31498e807af3412bd6df3d5d5ee8b37ec234f1c_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"demo/consumer.ml","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":41,"endLine":53,"snippet":{"text":"      expected := Int64.add !expected 1L"},"startColumn":19,"startLine":53}}}],"message":{"text":"Int64 arithmetic returns a freshly boxed int64. On hot paths (ring push/pop staging, merkle mix/update, demo tight loops) each add/mul/ sub/logxor is a minor allocation on top of any of_int boxing. Prefer unboxed int64 externals or keep heavy mixers off the steady-state path if the zero-allocation claim must hold strictly.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-int64-arith-hot-path"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"89a7b3f493d675bdeed4c6dbf95bce931e4167c5c818d962c79a81c3437029c94672f17a0e4f57886f32851a846911a22bd836006e7fa94119a44b937d1971d2_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"demo/consumer.ml","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":50,"endLine":65,"snippet":{"text":"       Region.store_rel hdr 4 (Int64.of_int chid);"},"startColumn":31,"startLine":65}}}],"message":{"text":"Int64.of_int allocates a boxed int64 on the OCaml heap outside init/create. On push/pop/tick/free/seti (and demo steady-state loops) this contradicts the \"zero OCaml heap allocation in steady state\" contract. Keep boxing on init-only paths, use [@@unboxed] externals, or accept and document the minor-allocation rate.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-int64-boxing-in-hot-path"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"c7fabc8eadbb637e96e3d21768f4727ee22e170b3858a079eb14018d3341118b06e627e400f270d02346f45fb479820bdf078da583c615d3b20eadd162d93b69_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"demo/consumer.ml","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":62,"endLine":66,"snippet":{"text":"       Region.store_rel hdr 3 (Int64.of_int (Unix.getpid ()));"},"startColumn":31,"startLine":66}}}],"message":{"text":"Int64.of_int allocates a boxed int64 on the OCaml heap outside init/create. On push/pop/tick/free/seti (and demo steady-state loops) this contradicts the \"zero OCaml heap allocation in steady state\" contract. Keep boxing on init-only paths, use [@@unboxed] externals, or accept and document the minor-allocation rate.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-int64-boxing-in-hot-path"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"d558bdadad7f91f617e7bdc4d3115f1f361af03ea67fb897bb4970e640c94c35fc82e0f0e473156587d71860be4857d2384071f6554f67fa5d71c614b0371708_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"demo/consumer.ml","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":70,"endLine":68,"snippet":{"text":"         Region.connect_attach (Int64.to_int (Region.load_acq hdr 1))"},"startColumn":32,"startLine":68}}}],"message":{"text":"A shared 64-bit counter is truncated to a 63-bit OCaml int. The monotone-never-wrap invariant holds for int64, but arithmetic after to_int wraps at 2^62; OCaml's (mod) then goes negative and indexing raises. Fine for realistic lifetimes, but the \"never wrapped\" claim in the docs must be qualified to 63 bits on the OCaml side.\n"},"propert