ush/pop staging, merkle mix/update, demo tight loops) each add/mul/ sub/logxor is a minor allocation on top of any of_int boxing. Prefer unboxed int64 externals or keep heavy mixers off the steady-state path if the zero-allocation claim must hold strictly.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-int64-arith-hot-path"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"7149f56d5e0a0778a56eefe7d0a3a61e6865174083b38c548a4eac5ec29e4ccda0a6602357b0e7fe859d5d1b4bfcca60e9454d07916451be6bd76a324620bd4e_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"lib/merkle.ml","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":75,"endLine":26,"snippet":{"text":"let mix2 a b = mix (Int64.logxor (mix a) (Int64.mul b 0xD6E8FEB86659FD93L))"},"startColumn":42,"startLine":26}}}],"message":{"text":"Int64 arithmetic returns a freshly boxed int64. On hot paths (ring push/pop staging, merkle mix/update, demo tight loops) each add/mul/ sub/logxor is a minor allocation on top of any of_int boxing. Prefer unboxed int64 externals or keep heavy mixers off the steady-state path if the zero-allocation claim must hold strictly.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-int64-arith-hot-path"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"7d60c15730047193a7478505c5655f52f7b94a5fbdbb9704e649582f413778d0ef315b7296963eff3cff195a3e05654355ef6400f25b32e47752764854b78c70_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"lib/merkle.ml","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":14,"endLine":39,"snippet":{"text":"  t.s.{!i} <- mix value;"},"startColumn":4,"startLine":39}}}],"message":{"text":"Plain (non-atomic) store on the Merkle update path. Initialization stores are expected and excluded; update publishes leaf→root with no release store and no acquire on the reader side, so a cross-process reader can observe the new root with stale children (or a torn path). Use store_rel on the root and load_acq on reads, or document a quiescence requirement.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-plain-store-to-shared-word"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"7d60c15730047193a7478505c5655f52f7b94a5fbdbb9704e649582f413778d0ef315b7296963eff3cff195a3e05654355ef6400f25b32e47752764854b78c70_1"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"lib/merkle.ml","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":16,"endLine":42,"snippet":{"text":"    t.s.{!i} <- mix2 t.s.{2 * !i} t.s.{(2 * !i) + 1}"},"startColumn":6,"startLine":42}}}],"message":{"text":"Plain (non-atomic) store on the Merkle update path. Initialization stores are expected and excluded; update publishes leaf→root with no release store and no acquire on the reader side, so a cross-process reader can observe the new root with stale children (or a torn path). Use store_rel on the root and load_acq on reads, or document a quiescence requirement.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-plain-store-to-shared-word"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"7d76c0fc7efd10fc1175a46e0caee17fddeaabb9fdbce72443cf8f1868a10d8ba2bdb2bb6d82b9ef39d6f81b90ac253094e645680d2812f2f19f495d131faa3d_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"lib/pmap.ml","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":19,"endLine":63,"snippet":{"text":"  log := i :: !log;"},"startColumn":3,"startLine":63}}}],"message":{"text":"The copy log is an OCaml heap list consed per copied node, and the version window is a heap list too. Every Pmap.set therefore allocates on the OCaml heap in steady state — the strongest form of the \"never allocate\" claim does not hold for Pmap. Either scope the claim to Ring/Arena/Vclock/Merkle, or move the log into the region.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-pmap-copy-log-heap-alloc"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"32378648f0ba5226ca94c8ff697ef8ca6fcbd7ca4b002a198e33de337b0f8c2a81ac10705b8c0d08e63ebcbe8a249e4f04be339913f678e943a82999308a516d_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"lib/pmap.ml","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":54,"endLine":134,"snippet":{"text":"         with Not_found -> failwith \"version retired\")"},"startColumn":28,"startLine":134}}}],"message":{"text":"failwith reachable at runtime: inventory the crash surface for steady-state operation. Region/Arena exhaustion are by design (preallocation contract violations), but a SCHED_FIFO/IPC failure path taking the process down may deserve a degraded-mode fallback.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-failwith-runtime-surface"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"942744c84168de8f19b1668e15074ef7b15c995cc5ca0f48aab82604381e9f06fcfea9d6770b3f14417eafca322e979bb7aacdb236bb02151b24b32d25f86e42_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"lib/region.ml","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":67,"endLine":65,"snippet":{"text":"    failwith \"region exhausted: size the slab before steady state\";"},"startColumn":5,"startLine":65}}}],"message":{"text":"failwith reachable at runtime: inventory the crash surface for steady-state operation. Region/Arena exhaustion are by design (preallocation contract violations), but a SCHED_FIFO/IPC failure path taking the process down may deserve a degraded-mode fallback.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-failwith-runtime-surface"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"f3db86c83e3ba422e6f05f99a8771ffc26ae1eb2275125ce3f71f5c5cc6c4a4af9d0f732ae23e317c866ab32f3a6b1579d61b9f5681d28f1857d75285d88a344_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"lib/ring.ml","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":35,"endLine":35,"snippet":{"text":"  s.{cap_ix} <- Int64.of_int slots;"},"startColumn":17,"startLine":35}}}],"message":{"text":"Int64.of_int boxes on an init/create path. Expected for one-time region setup (ring cap/width, vclock peer count, arena free-list chain). Not a steady-state concern; tracked separately from hot-path boxing so init noise does not hide push/pop allocations.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-int64-boxing-in-init"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"81a47882d7f4a368a34de9e1137cee82a8eabf12afb80bed57040bb9c9fe62ae704de9b23a6bf7cee84f84e28df6337590a0bc4e595b80bb85d53fd09ac7a057_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"lib/ring.ml","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":37,"endLine":36,"snippet":{"text":"  s.{width_ix} <- Int64.of_int width;"},"startColumn":19,"startLine":36}}}],"message":{"text":"Int64.of_int boxes on an init/create path. Expected for one-time region setup (ring cap/width, vclock peer count, arena free-list chain). Not a steady-state concern; tracked separately from hot-path boxing so init noise does not hide push/pop allocations.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-int64-boxing-in-init"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"85dbda0ceab0ac76e0ef3daf0e3f8affb88204f5f0f5803fb3d14a2bfc198a4b867dea38856ba4331cb661ad52aac6a15ef8d66ffdee31664143db86f1c6e060_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"lib/ring.ml","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":36,"endLine":42,"snippet":{"text":"  { s; cap = Int64.to_int s.{cap_ix}; width = Int64.to_int s.{width_ix} }"},"startColumn":14,"startLine":42}}}],"message":{"text":"Plain (non-acquire) read of a shared region word inside attach/config. Configuration words written at init are only safe to read after an explicit handshake (magic word / IPC) establishes happens-before. Single-owner Arena free-list walks are out of scope for this rule — they are not cross-process publication. Use Region.load_acq when the writer may still be initializing.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-plain-read-of-shared-config"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"839b2ab2afd540e208045a83b43b4713e86481890b223ec4add0c3ecd474fcc02485edd1aca60aff1b2fbd59331f4cd12e3a474625d293fddbf0ca473e19e617_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"lib/ring.ml","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":71,"endLine":42,"snippet":{"text":"  { s; cap = Int64.to_int s.{cap_ix}; width = Int64.to_int s.{width_ix} }"},"startColumn":47,"startLine":42}}}],"message":{"text":"Plain (non-acquire) read of a shared region word inside attach/config. Configuration words written at init are only safe to read after an explicit handshake (magic word / IPC) establishes happens-before. Single-owner Arena free-list walks are out of scope for this rule — they are not cross-process publication. Use Region.load_acq when the writer may still be initializing.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-plain-read-of-shared-config"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"ce05ae092eb59b6fd7f8cb6a65824157e8350f8ca51cf014501dead31107ba5e5d9446dd45f75c0294404377590c925811a1c8d774ffe236bd8b6a75cddcb8eb_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"lib/ring.ml","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":49,"endLine":44,"snippet":{"text":"let slot_base t i = header_words + (i mod t.cap) * t.width"},"startColumn":36,"startLine":44}}}],"message":{"text":"Modulo by t.cap: Ring.attach reads cap from the region with no validation, so attaching to a not-yet-initialized slice gives cap=0 and raises Division_by_zero at runtime instead of failing at attach. Validate cap > 0 (and width > 0) in attach.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-mod-capacity-without-zero-guard"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"d6eef561377c39f42f72aa250d4bf2db984e226fe50b719b88e77cb017542d878a8bd977ac9b2406444ab5b82c70e5d101e5b3471dd1c3cec9bb31e80fc6e289_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"lib/ring.ml","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":56,"endLine":48,"snippet":{"text":"  let tail = Int64.to_int (Region.load_acq t.s tail_ix) in"},"startColumn":14,"startLine":48}}}],"message":{"text":"A shared 64-bit counter is truncated to a 63-bit OCaml int. The monotone-never-wrap invariant holds for int64, but arithmetic after to_int wraps at 2^62; OCaml's (mod) then goes negative and indexing raises. Fine for realistic lifetimes, but the \"never wrapped\" claim in the docs must be qualified to 63 bits on the OCaml side.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-shared-counter-truncation"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"886e13b00d83eb940955e731feb1d89b58718c9358f37003c282b3b37afc1304bf1d9088d0a4869e7ddd76170f49d4fd834134f5c91fe09939113c2d9e8abb20_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"lib/ring.ml","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":56,"endLine":49,"snippet":{"text":"  let head = Int64.to_int (Region.load_acq t.s head_ix) in"},"startColumn":14,"startLine":49}}}],"message":{"text":"A shared 64-bit counter is truncated to a 63-bit OCaml int. The monotone-never-wrap invariant holds for int64, but arithmetic after to_int wraps at 2^62; OCaml's (mod) then goes negative and indexing raises. Fine for realistic lifetimes, but the \"never wrapped\" claim in the docs must be qualified to 63 bits on the OCaml side.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-shared-counter-truncation"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"8020d3d6a999e973b9a0b5dfc52a5d96edf81b49ed4e6640a58fdc8e68eb8818815a03baac33f8e4a13c2c2564e9daa242c034dd818c24182381ab2533ff95e8_0"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"lib/ring.ml","uriBaseId":"%SRCROOT%"},"region":{"endColumn":59,"endLine":54,"snippet":{"text":"    Region.store_rel t.s tail_ix (Int64.of_int (tail + 1));"},"startColumn":34,"startLine":54}}}],"message":{"text":"Int64.of_int allocates a boxed int64 on the OCaml heap outside init/create. On push/pop/tick/free/seti (and demo steady-state loops) this contradicts the \"zero OCaml heap allocation in steady state\" contract. Keep boxing on init-only paths, use [@@unboxed] externals, or accept and document the minor-allocation rate.\n"},"properties":{},"ruleId":"tools.opengrep.qnxml-int64-boxing-in-hot-path"},{"fingerprints":{"matchBasedId/v1":"886e13b00d83eb940955e731feb1d89b58718c